 r←Disconnect ns;out
⍝ Jarvis calls this when a WebSocket connection closes
⍝ ns - the connection's namespace (the same one Connect and Receive saw)
⍝ r  - Jarvis requires a result; it is not used
⍝ Forget the connection, and if the user had joined, tell everyone else they left
 :Hold 'Ex4Clients'
     Clients~←⊂ns.conx
 :EndHold
 :If 2=⌊ns.⎕NC⊂'User' ⍝ only announce people who joined
     out←⎕NS''
     out.(type user time)←'leave'ns.User Now
⍝ v20: out←(type: 'leave' ⋄ user: ns.User ⋄ time: Now)
     Clients ns.Server.WsSend out
 :EndIf
 r←0
